      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n`/v1/systemone` rejects an unknown field inside a question but silently drops an unknown field on the request itself (`OpenAIBaseModel` allows extras). A client using a sibling dialect's field, for example Jev/SystemOne's `assets` map for images, gets answers scored without its images and no error. This applies the question-level rule to the request.\n\n## Claims\n\n- A `/v1/systemone` request with a field outside `StructuredDecisionRequest` returns 400 `unknown field(s) [...]` before admission, instead of being read without it.\n\n## Validation\n\n**Real model.** `Cloudflare/clef` (27B, FP8, loaded as `ClefFlashForJointSchema`) on one L40S, v0.32.1rc0 commit `2365177d` with this change applied:\n\n| Request | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 20 valid requests (text, JSON, images, 16K truncation) | 200 | 200 |\n| Image request in Jev form: `assets` map, no `images` | 200, scored without the image | 400 `unknown field(s) ['assets']` |\n| Valid request plus `\"seed\": 7` | 200 | 400 `unknown field(s) ['seed']` |\n\n**Tests.** `test_systemone_rejects_unknown_request_fields` posts a request with `assets` through the router and asserts the 400 and that nothing was admitted. It fails without the change.\n\n```bash\npytest tests/entrypoints/generate/structured_decisions/test_decisions.py \\\n  tests/entrypoints/generate/structured_decisions/test_question_types.py \\\n  tests/entrypoints/generate/structured_decisions/test_strategies.py\n# 111 passed\n```\n\n## Details\n\n- **Compatibility:** clients that send extra fields today start getting 400. The endpoint is new (#59299, #60677), and the original example in #59299 sent `\"seed\": 7`, which this would now reject, so callers copying it will need to drop it. That is the intended trade: an ignored field on this endpoint changes what the model reads (media, instructions) without any signal.\n- `/v1/decisions` is unchanged; it follows the OpenAI schema and its own validation.\n- Docs: the request-fields section states the rule.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
